Earth surface and cloud imagery

NASA Visible Earth / NASA Goddard Space Flight Center, The Blue Marble.
https://eoimages.gsfc.nasa.gov/images/imagerecords/57000/57730/land_ocean_ice_2048.png
https://eoimages.gsfc.nasa.gov/images/imagerecords/57000/57747/cloud_combined_2048.jpg

The local JPEG reductions are shared with this repository's 550W theme.
The native material maps the surface to an icy-blue palette; cloud cover is a
separate translucent sphere. Images are bundled locally with no network loads.
NASA does not endorse this project.

Lunar color and elevation maps

NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio, CGI Moon Kit (Ernie Wright).
LRO Camera (LROC) and Lunar Orbiter Laser Altimeter (LOLA) datasets.
https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/4720/
https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/vis/a000000/a004700/a004720/lroc_color_poles_1k.jpg
https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/vis/a000000/a004700/a004720/ldem_3_8bit.jpg

Images are bundled locally. A lunar normal map is calculated once from the
elevation map; the native lighting supplies the theme's charcoal/red palette.
